From 1be25f24c5484db43afebfb11c7f5d3c43518e03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:44:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(trace): Centerline keeps a bend drawn round in a
 thick stroke (ADR-394)

Centerline rebuilt any bend whose two straight legs pointed at a corner,
so a thick stroke's rounded bend (the bottom of a wave, the shoulder of a
letter) came out as a V. Before rebuilding a corner, the sharpener now
reads the ink at the rebuilt vertex. On a drawn corner the vertex sits on
the pen's path with the stroke's full width of ink around it. On a curve
it stands off the path, and the ink there is thinner by about as much as
it stands off. Where the vertex lost more than half its distance from the
traced line (and more than 0.6 px), the bend keeps its curve. Drawn
corners are still rebuilt. The contour tracer calls the same sharpener
without the new option, so outlines are unchanged.

Measured against the base (85ee406) with the audit's centreline bench:
- 21-stroke corpus: mean distance from the true centre 0.254 -> 0.250 px,
  mean 95th percentile 0.43 -> 0.39 px, share of the true centre covered
  99.84% -> 100%. Only the three waves change: the 8 px wave's largest
  gap 2.24 -> 0.43 px (95th percentile 1.02 -> 0.23 px, coverage 97.3% ->
  100%), the 4 px wave's 1.27 -> 0.60 px, the 2 px wave's 0.81 -> 0.49 px.
- 290 synthetic bends (3-12 px strokes, 45-150 degree turns; sharp,
  mitred and filleted paths): mean local error 1.25 -> 0.85 px. 88 bends
  improve by more than 0.1 px; one gets worse, a 3 px stroke's small
  fillet (0.60 -> 0.89 px).
- In-repo regression bar: unchanged.
- Contour presets (Line Art, Smooth, Sharp, Edge Detection): identical
  output, timing aside, on the 48 audit corpus traces and the 8 traces of
  the dragon and logo.
- Dragon: 2,518 paths either way, 66,690 -> 67,610 vertices. Logo: 74
  paths, 2,552 -> 2,588 vertices.

